From: pocket_vm developers <pocket-vm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] um: vector: allow a static link without the IP transports

UML_NET_VECTOR selects MAY_HAVE_RUNTIME_DEPS unconditionally, and
STATIC_LINK depends on !MAY_HAVE_RUNTIME_DEPS, so enabling any vector
networking forces a dynamically linked UML.

The dependency is real but it belongs to two of the eight transports.
Only gre and l2tpv3 address their peer by name, and only they call
getaddrinfo(3), which a statically linked binary cannot resolve through
NSS.  raw and tap name an interface, fd inherits a descriptor, and bess
and vde connect to a filesystem path; none of them resolve anything.

Move the select onto a new option covering just those two transports.
The default is y, so an existing configuration is unchanged; turning it
off keeps the remaining six transports and permits STATIC_LINK.
---
 arch/um/drivers/Kconfig | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/drivers/Kconfig b/arch/um/drivers/Kconfig
index 6a0354c..be7fb7f 100644
--- a/arch/um/drivers/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/Kconfig
@@ -126,7 +126,6 @@ menu "UML Network Devices"
 
 config UML_NET_VECTOR
 	bool "Vector I/O high performance network devices"
-	select MAY_HAVE_RUNTIME_DEPS
 	help
 	  This User-Mode Linux network driver uses multi-message send
 	  and receive functions. The host running the UML guest must have
@@ -137,6 +136,23 @@ config UML_NET_VECTOR
 	  and sample configurations, see
 	  <file:Documentation/virt/uml/user_mode_linux_howto_v2.rst>.
 
+config UML_NET_VECTOR_IP_TRANSPORTS
+	bool "GRE and L2TPv3 transports"
+	depends on UML_NET_VECTOR
+	default y
+	select MAY_HAVE_RUNTIME_DEPS
+	help
+	  The gre and l2tpv3 transports address their peer by name and
+	  resolve it with getaddrinfo(3), which needs NSS.  A statically
+	  linked UML cannot load NSS modules, so selecting these transports
+	  forces a dynamically linked binary.
+
+	  Say N to keep the raw, tap, bess, fd and vde transports while
+	  allowing STATIC_LINK.  Each of those names its peer by interface,
+	  file descriptor or filesystem path and resolves nothing.
+
+	  If unsure, say Y.
+
 endmenu
 
 config VIRTIO_UML
